{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"4f42c5bd27a1f934","name":"card_event_focused_attack_ger","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Germany/WinterWar/events/card_event_focused_attack_ger","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"FOCUSED ATTACK","text":"Your infantry and tanks get +1+1 for each unit type you control.","flavorText":"The Battle of Kasserine Pass was fought in February 1943 in Tunisia between the Allied forces, comprising primarily inexperienced US troops, and the seasoned German and Italian forces. It marked the first major confrontation between the Western Allies and the Axis forces in North Africa. The US forces, under the command of General Lloyd Fredendall, encountered significant difficulties due to lack of experience, inadequate leadership, and poor coordination among their units. The Germans, led by General Erwin Rommel, capitalized on these weaknesses, employing effective combined arms tactics and demonstrating their superiority in maneuver warfare. For the US Army, the battle served as a learning experience. It revealed its deficiencies in command, logistics and tactics, leading to improvements in the US Army training, leadership and coordination which contributed to their growing strength in the later stages of the war.","faction":"Germany","type":"order","rarity":"Common","cost":6,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_focused_attack_ger","title":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_focused_attack_ger_title","SourceString":"FOCUSED ATTACK","LocalizedString":"FOCUSED ATTACK"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Germany","kredits":6,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_focused_attack_ger_text","SourceString":"Your infantry and tanks get +1+1 for each unit type you control.","LocalizedString":"Your infantry and tanks get +1+1 for each unit type you control."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_focused_attack_ger_history","SourceString":"The Battle of Kasserine Pass was fought in February 1943 in Tunisia between the Allied forces, comprising primarily inexperienced US troops, and the seasoned German and Italian forces. It marked the first major confrontation between the Western Allies and the Axis forces in North Africa. The US forces, under the command of General Lloyd Fredendall, encountered significant difficulties due to lack of experience, inadequate leadership, and poor coordination among their units. The Germans, led by General Erwin Rommel, capitalized on these weaknesses, employing effective combined arms tactics and demonstrating their superiority in maneuver warfare. For the US Army, the battle served as a learning experience. It revealed its deficiencies in command, logistics and tactics, leading to improvements in the US Army training, leadership and coordination which contributed to their growing strength in the later stages of the war.","LocalizedString":"The Battle of Kasserine Pass was fought in February 1943 in Tunisia between the Allied forces, comprising primarily inexperienced US troops, and the seasoned German and Italian forces. It marked the first major confrontation between the Western Allies and the Axis forces in North Africa. The US forces, under the command of General Lloyd Fredendall, encountered significant difficulties due to lack of experience, inadequate leadership, and poor coordination among their units. The Germans, led by General Erwin Rommel, capitalized on these weaknesses, employing effective combined arms tactics and demonstrating their superiority in maneuver warfare. For the US Army, the battle served as a learning experience. It revealed its deficiencies in command, logistics and tactics, leading to improvements in the US Army training, leadership and coordination which contributed to their growing strength in the later stages of the war."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::WinterWar","isReserved":true,"soun